erable0B0P","text":"Transferable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"\n","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/navigationdocument(_:preview:)-1oxp9"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView":{"title":"Interaction_DragView","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drags a layer in any direction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":" patch, which wires its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"output "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card snaps back to its resting position."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/navigationDocument(_:preview:)-1oxp9":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"navigationDocument"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"D"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"I1","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"I2","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"D","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"preview","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SharePreview","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI12SharePreviewV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"I1","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"I2","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"View","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/navigationdocument(_:preview:)-1oxp9","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/navigationDocument(_:preview:)-1oxp9","kind":"symbol","title":"navigationDocument(_:preview:)","type":"topic","abstract":[]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"title":"Swami","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swami","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"}}}